,
105
]. This approach surpasses the constraints of cell culture models, allowing for the direct observation of LCD behavior amidst the complexities of tissue architecture, cellular crowding, and physiological signaling. Such insights are essential for comprehending the physiological and pathological roles of LCDs.
These emerging directions, in conjunction with the advanced application of established methodologies, are poised to address pivotal unresolved questions in LCD research. These include the spatiotemporal regulation of phase separation in vivo, the causal relationship between LCD heterogeneity and disease, and the rational design of therapies targeting LCDs.
